{
  "id": "68f2581a-e7ff-4469-9e3c-4febf7ce7f3e",
  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "data": {
    "body": "Consider the series\n$\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} a_k=\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} (\\dfrac{k}{k^2+2k+3})$sin($\\dfrac{1}{k}$).\nWe conclude\n",
    "solution": [
      3
    ],
    "answerChoices": [
      {
        "id": "401511de-998e-4989-8bda-4826af4b7d98",
        "index": 0,
        "body": "the series is convergent since $\\lim_{k\\to\\infty} a_k = 0$.",
        "questionId": "68f2581a-e7ff-4469-9e3c-4febf7ce7f3e",
        "stats": {
          "count": 5
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "63fd9453-882b-49b8-91b7-f013c9f35197",
        "index": 1,
        "body": "the series is divergent by Ratio test since $\\lim_{k\\to\\infty} \\left|\\frac{a_{k+1}}{a_k}\\right| = 1$. ",
        "questionId": "68f2581a-e7ff-4469-9e3c-4febf7ce7f3e",
        "stats": {
          "count": 5
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "ee447409-7d4f-4201-a31c-c88fe00cd806",
        "index": 2,
        "body": "the series is divergent by the Limit Comparison test since $\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{k}{k^2} = \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{k}$. ",
        "questionId": "68f2581a-e7ff-4469-9e3c-4febf7ce7f3e",
        "stats": {
          "count": 14
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "cf8c6a01-c01f-4d67-afc7-1d64b346d55d",
        "index": 3,
        "body": "the series is convergent by the Limit Comparison test since $\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{k^2}$. ",
        "questionId": "68f2581a-e7ff-4469-9e3c-4febf7ce7f3e",
        "stats": {
          "count": 34
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "2ced7a1d-daff-4c96-b8f5-6d95101170af",
        "index": 4,
        "body": "the series is divergent by the Test for Divergence since $\\lim_{k\\to\\infty} a_k$ does not exist. ",
        "questionId": "68f2581a-e7ff-4469-9e3c-4febf7ce7f3e",
        "stats": {
          "count": 2
        },
        "resources": []
      }
    ]
